WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.900
The Llama family.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:08.600
Meta's open-weight family is the base for most industry fine-tuning, and its design became the standard.

3
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:12.000
LLaMA is Meta's open-weight family.

4
00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:17.867
When a company adapts a model on private data, the base is more often a Llama than anything else.

5
00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:25.367
Its design is GPT-2's skeleton, with a few upgrades that nearly every open model now copies.

6
00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:27.667
Here is the block.

7
00:00:27.967 --> 00:00:29.860
Tokens come in as embeddings.

8
00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.733
Positions are added later, inside attention.

9
00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:35.647
Each sublayer is preceded by RMSNorm.

10
00:00:35.647 --> 00:00:41.933
Attention uses RoPE, and later versions share key and value heads to shrink the KV cache.

11
00:00:42.233 --> 00:00:46.267
The feed-forward network uses SwiGLU, and there are no bias terms.

12
00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:50.467
Side by side, the four upgrades are easy to see.

13
00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:53.067
RMSNorm replaces LayerNorm.

14
00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:55.200
RoPE replaces learned positions.

15
00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.133
SwiGLU replaces GELU.

16
00:00:57.433 --> 00:00:59.133
And the bias terms disappear.

17
00:01:00.333 --> 00:01:02.500
You can read all this from a config file.

18
00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:05.354
We download the config for Llama 3.

19
00:01:05.354 --> 00:01:05.500
2.

20
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:07.475
Then print four fields.

21
00:01:07.475 --> 00:01:10.607
The activation is silu, the gate in SwiGLU.

22
00:01:10.607 --> 00:01:15.633
There is an RMSNorm epsilon, a RoPE theta, and eight key value heads.

23
00:01:16.833 --> 00:01:19.133
Here is why this vocabulary matters.

24
00:01:19.433 --> 00:01:25.033
Mission notes cannot leave your network, so the assistant is a LoRA fine-tune of a Llama base.

25
00:01:25.333 --> 00:01:27.233
It is served on your own GPU.

26
00:01:27.533 --> 00:01:33.333
Quantization, KV cache growth and context stretching are all read straight from the config.

27
00:01:34.533 --> 00:01:35.272
Let's recap.

28
00:01:35.272 --> 00:01:38.533
LLaMA's open weights are the base of most fine-tunes.

29
00:01:38.833 --> 00:01:40.900
It uses RMSNorm and RoPE.

30
00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.867
SwiGLU and no biases.

31
00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:46.864
And the config file shows any model's anatomy in seconds.

32
00:01:46.864 --> 00:01:47.967
Next up: Mistral.
